{"sourceSha256": "2820726ae26f60bd10be85e1e4008c9a63d8f6f860fd34ae34db9bdddae59700", "text": "Patient:\n\nNurse:\n\nPatient:\n\nNurse:\n\nPatient:\n\nNurse:\n\nPatient:\n\nNurse:\n\nPatient:\nNurse:\n\nPatient:\n\nNo... That's pretty much... Oh,...there’s one thing. | have been\nrestricting my fluid intake. | am scared thar it will deteriorate my\ncondition.\n\nSo, when you say restricting, do you mean you haven't had any fluid at\nall?\n\noh no, | mean I just have sips of water.\n\nAlright. So based on our consultation, | believe that you are suffering\nfrom urge incontinence. Do you have any prior information about\nthis?\n\n(sounding alarmed) No... | am nor sure... Is it serious? Are their\ntreatment options available?\n\nUrinary incontinence is a common problem, especially in women. It\nhappens when there is involuntary leakage of urine from the bladder.\nIts prevalence increases as people get older. That being said, let me\nassure you that it is easily treatable with medication and several\ntreatment options. And it is not something to be alarmed about.\n(sighs) ah...ok. So, what kinds of treatment options are available for\nme?\n\nIn addition to the medication, treatments like Bladder training and\nPelvic Floor muscle exercises will assist in managing your condition.\nFor this, | would advise secing a urologist who specialises in treating\nincontinence of the bladder. Would it be okay if 1 can schedule an\nappointment for you tomorrow at the same time?\n\nAh, thank you! Would be appreciated.\n\nThat's alright. In the meantime, | will suggest you to use to use\ndisposable undergarments and continence pads so that your leak can\nbe managed and it does not hold you back from activities you enjoy.\nHow does that sound?\n\nYes, that would be hugely helpful. Thank you, nurse.", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Patient:\n\nNurse:\n\nPatient:\n\nNurse:\n\nPatient:\n\nNurse:\n\nPatient:\n\nNurse:\n\nPatient:\nNurse:\n\nPatient:\n\nNo... That's pretty much... Oh,...there’s one thing. | have been\nrestricting my fluid intake. | am scared thar it will deteriorate my\ncondition.\n\nSo, when you say restricting, do you mean you haven't had any fluid at\nall?\n\noh no, | mean I just have sips of water.\n\nAlright. So based on our consultation, | believe that you are suffering\nfrom urge incontinence. Do you have any prior information about\nthis?\n\n(sounding alarmed) No... | am nor sure... Is it serious? Are their\ntreatment options available?\n\nUrinary incontinence is a common problem, especially in women. It\nhappens when there is involuntary leakage of urine from the bladder.\nIts prevalence increases as people get older. That being said, let me\nassure you that it is easily treatable with medication and several\ntreatment options. And it is not something to be alarmed about.\n(sighs) ah...ok. So, what kinds of treatment options are available for\nme?\n\nIn addition to the medication, treatments like Bladder training and\nPelvic Floor muscle exercises will assist in managing your condition.\nFor this, | would advise secing a urologist who specialises in treating\nincontinence of the bladder. Would it be okay if 1 can schedule an\nappointment for you tomorrow at the same time?\n\nAh, thank you! Would be appreciated.\n\nThat's alright. In the meantime, | will suggest you to use to use\ndisposable undergarments and continence pads so that your leak can\nbe managed and it does not hold you back from activities you enjoy.\nHow does that sound?\n\nYes, that would be hugely helpful. Thank you, nurse.", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2328.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Patient:", "lines": [{"text": "Patient:", "x": 0.13617, "y": 0.07714, "width": 0.07259, "height": 0.01429, "confidence": 0.961, "words": [{"text": "Patient:", "x": 0.13617, "width": 0.07259, "confidence": 0.961}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Nurse:", "lines": [{"text": "Nurse:", "x": 0.13617, "y": 0.15107, "width": 0.061, "height": 